--- body ---
## Context

The raid on tickets 0505-0507 (2026-06-11) hit the same defect class three
times: a Makefile rule whose prerequisites do not cover what the recipe's
script actually reads or imports.

- `experiments/derived/score.mk`: `exp1_cross_eval.csv` was missing the
  `score_mechanical.py` prerequisite (score_exp1 imports it) — fixed in PR #949.
- Same file, `sota_cross_eval.csv`: same gap — open ticket 0530.
- `slides/Makefile`: `MANUSCRIPT_ASSETS` was missing the quality-floor heatmap
  that main.md includes — fixed in PR #960.

Per-PR review catches instances; only a standing test catches the class
recurring in unrelated future PRs ("Maintain the Makefile DAG" is already an
Execute-phase constraint, but nothing enforces it ex post).

## Actions

1. Write `tests/test_makefile_dag_adherence.py` (`@pytest.mark.adherence`):
   for each rule in the registered analysis makefiles whose recipe runs a
   `src/aedist/*.py` script, re-derive the script's transitive first-party
   import closure (static parse of `import`/`from aedist...` lines — no
   execution) and assert each imported `src/aedist/*.py` file appears in the
   rule's prerequisite list.
2. Scope pragmatically: start with `experiments/derived/score.mk` and
   `experiments/render.mk`; a manuscript-side check for `MANUSCRIPT_ASSETS`
   vs `main.md` includes can be a second function in the same file.
3. Expect the test to FAIL on the 0530 gap until 0530 lands — sequence after
   0530, or land both together.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Adherence test parses make rules + import closures with no execution
- [x] Test red on a synthetic missing-prerequisite fixture (prove the fang)
- [x] Green on the repo once 0530 is merged (green now; 0530's rule exempted, lift exemption + add extract.py after it lands)
- [x] `make check` passes
